 "_note": "Centre drill (combined drill and countersink) dimensions as printed by each publisher. Inch fractions are written as their exact decimals (3/64 = 0.046875); decimals are as printed. Field meanings: body = body (shank) diameter; pilot = pilot (drill) diameter; pilot_len = pilot (drill) length as printed; bell = bell (protecting chamfer) diameter; cone = largest diameter of the 60 degree countersink of type B, where the 120 degree protecting chamfer starts; l_min / l_max = pilot length range; r_max / r_min = radius of the type R profile. Built by scripts/build_refdata.py into refdata.json (section centredrills).",
 "sources": {
  "ICS": {"publisher": "ICS Cutting Tools", "title": "Catalogue page 114, combined drills and countersinks (plain type 60 deg; plain type 82 and 90 deg)", "url": "https://www.icscuttingtools.com/catalog/page_114.pdf", "accessed": "2026-11-11", "note": "Maker. Size 00 drill diameter is printed 0.25 (a misprint for .025: the drill length column prints .025 and the body is 1/8); transcribed here as .025."},
  "GREENFIELD": {"publisher": "Greenfield Industries (Cleveland), catalogue page via ME Campbell", "title": "Style 217 plain type and style 217B bell type combined drill and countersink", "url": "https://www.mecampbell.com/media/pdf/GREENFE00009_131.pdf", "accessed": "2026-11-11", "note": "Maker. Decimal inch to 4 places. Sizes 00 and 0 print a drill length longer than the drill diameter (.0300, .0380)."},
  "MICHIGAN": {"publisher": "Michigan Drill", "title": "Catalogue list 582/585/590 combined drills and countersinks, plain type (60, 82 and 90 deg), and list 587 bell type", "url": "https://default.assets-generalfactory-prod.roccommercecloud.com/assets%2F85ee570bdd31d33d0baea72969a996c8/Michigan_Drill_582_1_Catalog.pdf", "accessed": "2026-11-11", "note": "Maker. Plain type: body and drill diameter only (no drill length column). Bell type (list 587, https://default.assets-generalfactory-prod.roccommercecloud.com/assets%2F9e19334a7c7881853e50173b60b4f741/Michigan_Drill_587_11_Catalog.pdf): body, 'drill dia. and length' in one column, bell diameter; no size 19."},
  "EXACT": {"publisher": "Exact Tooling", "title": "Combined drill and countersinks, bell type (60 deg with 120 deg chamfer)", "url": "https://exacttooling.com/pages/cuttingtools-solidround-combineddrills-countersinks-belltype", "accessed": "2026-11-11", "note": "Distributor (Magafor and own brand). Sizes 11 to 20."},
  "LINEAR": {"publisher": "Linear Tools (data sheet LDS 1082, via Farnell)", "title": "Centre drills: metric DIN 333 / ISO 866, inch short series, bell type, radius type", "url": "https://www.farnell.com/datasheets/2804844.pdf", "accessed": "2026-11-11", "note": "UK maker/distributor. Metric table: d, D, l, L; the single l printed equals the minimum of the ZPS range and of ISO 2540, so it is recorded as l_min. Inch short series and bell type print a pilot length l longer than the US makers' drill length (British BS 328 practice); shown as printed, a different measure or a different design."},
  "ZPS": {"publisher": "ZPS-FN (Czech Republic)", "title": "Centre drills 60 deg form A, DIN 333A, HSS (VS92010) and form R, DIN 333R (VS93010)", "url": "https://zps-fn.cz/en/drills/detail/centre-drills-60-form-a,-din-333a,-high-speed-steel-hss", "accessed": "2026-11-11", "note": "Maker. Table D, d, l1, l2 (l2 printed as a range). Form R page: https://zps-fn.cz/en/drills/detail/centre-drills-60-form-r,-din-333r,-high-speed-steel-hss . Symbols are not defined on the page; D is read as the body diameter and d as the pilot diameter (they match ISO 866 and ISO 2541)."},
  "ISO2540": {"publisher": "ISO (public preview of ISO 2540:2016 on standards.iteh.ai)", "title": "ISO 2540:2016 Centre drills for centre holes with protecting chamfer - Type B, Table 1", "url": "https://cdn.standards.iteh.ai/samples/64194/2a14d980bea94904bca92bcfb2a6daf7/ISO-2540-2016.pdf", "accessed": "2026-11-11", "note": "The standard's own table (pilot d, shank d1, countersink d2, l max and min, L). The 1973 edition preview prints the same numbers; it is the same standard, so it is not counted as a second source."},
  "ISO2541": {"publisher": "ISO (public preview of ISO 2541:2016 on standards.iteh.ai)", "title": "ISO 2541:2016 Centre drills for centre holes with radius form - Type R, Table 1", "url": "https://cdn.standards.iteh.ai/samples/64195/e9e87d5aa48d4bd58e7ea8018989f847/ISO-2541-2016.pdf", "accessed": "2026-11-11", "note": "Read from a text extract whose column headings did not line up with the numbers: pilot and shank diameters are clear; the radius columns are taken as the last two numbers of each row (max, min) and should be checked against the printed table."},
  "TECWERK": {"publisher": "Nordwest Handel (TECWERK brand)", "title": "Centre drill bit DIN 333 shape B, nominal 3.15 mm, HSS", "url": "https://www.nordwest-tecwerk.com/en/products/machining/drill-bits/centre-drill-bits/centre-drill-bit-din-333-shape-b-hss-w-protection-lowering-right-cutting-tecwerk", "accessed": "2026-11-11", "note": "Distributor. Only the 3.15 mm size has dimensions: shank 11.2 mm, overall length 60 mm."}
